{"code":"51-7021.00","title":"Furniture Finishers","description":"Shape, finish, and refinish damaged, worn, or used furniture or new high-grade furniture to specified color or finish.","jobZone":2,"kinds":{"R":{"score":7,"share":0.5714},"I":{"score":1.45,"share":0.0429},"A":{"score":2.93,"share":0.1838},"S":{"score":1.25,"share":0.0238},"E":{"score":1,"share":0},"C":{"score":2.87,"share":0.1781}},"highPoints":["R","A","C"],"tasks":[{"id":14265,"text":"Confer with customers to determine furniture colors or finishes.","core":false,"importance":4.34,"relevance":48.86,"frequency":4.53},{"id":14251,"text":"Brush, spray, or hand-rub finishing ingredients, such as paint, oil, stain, or wax, onto and into wood grain and apply lacquer or other sealers.","core":true,"importance":4.28,"relevance":95.81,"frequency":5.67},{"id":14254,"text":"Fill and smooth cracks or depressions, remove marks and imperfections, and repair broken parts, using plastic or wood putty, glue, nails, or screws.","core":true,"importance":4.26,"relevance":79.45,"frequency":4.96},{"id":14252,"text":"Smooth, shape, and touch up surfaces to prepare them for finishing, using sandpaper, pumice stones, steel wool, chisels, sanders, or grinders.","core":true,"importance":4.24,"relevance":81.88,"frequency":5.31},{"id":14263,"text":"Remove accessories prior to finishing, and mask areas that should not be exposed to finishing processes or substances.","core":true,"importance":4.2,"relevance":82.29,"frequency":4.94},{"id":14259,"text":"Remove old finishes and damaged or deteriorated parts, using hand tools, stripping tools, sandpaper, steel wool, abrasives, solvents, or dip baths.","core":true,"importance":4.17,"relevance":85.23,"frequency":5.02},{"id":14258,"text":"Recommend woods, colors, finishes, and furniture styles, using knowledge of wood products, fashions, and styles.","core":false,"importance":4.11,"relevance":50.41,"frequency":4.49},{"id":14264,"text":"Treat warped or stained surfaces to restore original contours and colors.","core":true,"importance":4.08,"relevance":77.15,"frequency":4.74},{"id":14253,"text":"Select appropriate finishing ingredients such as paint, stain, lacquer, shellac, or varnish, depending on factors such as wood hardness and surface type.","core":true,"importance":4.06,"relevance":80.08,"frequency":5.45},{"id":14250,"text":"Mix finish ingredients to obtain desired colors or shades.","core":true,"importance":4.04,"relevance":77.09,"frequency":4.78},{"id":14262,"text":"Wash surfaces to prepare them for finish application.","core":false,"importance":4.03,"relevance":59.38,"frequency":4.87},{"id":14267,"text":"Remove excess solvent, using cloths soaked in paint thinner.","core":true,"importance":4.01,"relevance":72.51,"frequency":4.49},{"id":14260,"text":"Follow blueprints to produce specific designs.","core":false,"importance":4,"relevance":48.92,"frequency":4.74},{"id":14257,"text":"Paint metal surfaces electrostatically, or by using a spray gun or other painting equipment.","core":false,"importance":3.95,"relevance":45.35,"frequency":4.49},{"id":14256,"text":"Examine furniture to determine the extent of damage or deterioration, and to decide on the best method for repair or restoration.","core":true,"importance":3.92,"relevance":85.74,"frequency":4.89},{"id":14255,"text":"Distress surfaces with woodworking tools or abrasives before staining to create an antique appearance, or rub surfaces to bring out highlights and shadings.","core":true,"importance":3.87,"relevance":80.3,"frequency":4.25},{"id":14268,"text":"Stencil, gild, emboss, mark, or paint designs or borders to reproduce the original appearance of restored pieces, or to decorate new pieces.","core":true,"importance":3.86,"relevance":70,"frequency":3.72},{"id":14261,"text":"Disassemble items to prepare them for finishing, using hand tools.","core":true,"importance":3.85,"relevance":67.86,"frequency":4.55},{"id":14266,"text":"Replace or refurbish upholstery of items, using tacks, adhesi